        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="RES01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Nicolas</forename>
                        <surname>Restif</surname>
                        <addName>Edme</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1734-10-23">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1806-02-03"/>
                    <occupation>author</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>There are three entries to 'Restiff' in the first three months of 1793.  They are odd as it is rare for Godwin to 
  confer two consonants at the end of a person's name and, in this case, only one is called for.  It is certainly possible
  that Retif was in London at this time although there is no evidence to support this. He was the author 
  of <title>Les nuits de Paris, ou Le Spectateur nocturne</title> (1788-1794, 8  volumes).</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
        </body>
